      <p>The editor can run an agent you already use as a separate program, and lend it the editor's DITA operations. The agent keeps its own sign-in and its own model; the editor supplies the tools and the limits.</p>
      <p>This works with any agent that speaks the Agent Client Protocol. Claude Code, Codex and Gemini CLI are the ones most people have.</p>
      <h2 id="before-you-start" class="group scroll-mt-20">Before you start<a href="#before-you-start" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Turn on the integration server, which is how the agent reaches the editor's tools. Select <strong>File &gt; Preferences &gt; Server</strong> and enable it.</p>
      <h2 id="starting-a-session" class="group scroll-mt-20">Starting a session<a href="#starting-a-session" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
